    "fileId": 18099,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Proposed nomenclature for the spectrum of neurofibromatosis type&nbsp;1&ndash;associated peripheral nerve sheath tumours</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Reprinted, with permission, from Miettinen MM, Antonescu CR, Fletcher CDM, et al. Histopathologic evaluation of atypical neurofibromatous tumors and their transformation into malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor in patients with neurofibromatosis 1-a consensus overview. Hum Pathol. 2017 Sep;67:1-10. PMID: 28551330.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; \" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Proposed definition</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>NF</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A benign Schwann cell neoplasm with thin and often wavy nuclei, wispy cell processes, and a myxoid to collagenous (shredded-carrots) matrix; immunohistochemistry includes extensive but not diffuse S100 and SOX10 positivity and a lattice-like CD34+ fibroblastic network</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Plexiform NF</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">A diffusely enlarging NF replacing a nerve, often involving multiple nerve fascicles, delineated by EMA+ perineurial cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>NF with atypia (ancient NF)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">NF with atypia alone, most commonly manifesting as scattered bizarre nuclei</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Cellular NF</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">NF with hypercellularity but retained NF architecture and no mitoses</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>ANNUBP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A Schwann cell neoplasm with at least 2&nbsp;of the following 4&nbsp;features: cytological atypia, loss of neurofibroma architecture, hypercellularity, &lt;&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (&lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;<span style=\"\">HPF<sup>a</sup>)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">MPNST, low-grade</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">A tumour with features of ANNUBP but with mitotic counts of 1.5&ndash;4.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (3&ndash;9&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;<span style=\"\">HPF<sup>a</sup>) </span>and no necrosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>MPNST, high-grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 541.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"723\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">MPNST with &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (&ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;<span style=\"\">HPF<sup>a</sup>)</span> or 1.5&ndash;4.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (3&ndash;9&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;<span style=\"\">HPF<sup>a</sup>) </span>combined with necrosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ANNUBP, atypical neurofibromatous neoplasm of uncertain biological potential; HPF, high-power field; MPNST, malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour; NF, neurofibroma.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>1&nbsp;mm&nbsp;= approximately 5&nbsp;HPF of 0.51&nbsp;mm in diameter.</p>",
